-### 3.5 Squelch tail elimination
+### 3.5 Channel squelch and tail elimination
+
+An FM channel's byte 0x37 selects its squelch: 0 follows the radio default, 1-21 maps to the radio's 1-9 control
+(the codeplug scale is qdmr's 1-10 doubled), and RadioFoundry's 22 selects level 0, always open. Other values above
+21 read as 10, as before. A channel load, Clear changes and a restart restore this stored value; a temporary change
+that returns to it clears the temporary flag. Digital channels and the VFO continue to use the radio default. An
+always-open channel does not make a scan stop on noise alone: the scan still needs a carrier.
 
 No reverse burst or tone-loss signal from the other station is acted on yet; closing early on CTCSS loss conflicts
 with the tone debounce (8 polls) that keeps fades from chopping audio.
